    "ADO-EVENT"
  ],
  "description": "ADO-ASYNC adAsyncFetch on a source that is slow to fetch (the first card's join was too fast): a client static read-only recordset over a six-way cross join of K returning one row per combination (10^6 rows) opened with adAsyncFetch, then a second with adAsyncFetchNonBlocking; a RecordsetEvents sink on each; State, RecordCount and AbsolutePosition right after Open and after pauses of 200, 1000 and 3000 ms (timestamped); MoveLast; the FetchProgress and FetchComplete events recorded. Asks whether row fetching is asynchronous on this provider and when events arrive.",
  "callerSurface": "native-idispatch/x64",
  "invokeLcid": 1033,
